,"closed_at":null},"comments":4,"created_at":"2025-01-18T16:23:03Z","updated_at":"2026-08-06T08:28:46Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101764","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101764","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101764.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101764.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch in priority.\r\n\r\nRelevant fixes are cherry-picked for stable branches as needed by maintainers.\r\n\r\nTo speed up the contribution process and avoid CI errors, please set up pre-commit hooks locally:\r\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/development/code_style_guidelines.html\r\n-->\r\nFixes #101073, fixes #103460, and fixes #116206. I moved the loading order to be after the `ScriptServer.init`. This may or may not introduce bugs relating to `Translation`s so some further testing might be required. I am not well-acquainted with the main loading process, so I probably missed some things.\r\n\r\nWhen loaded in the `ProjectSettings`, any class that extended `Translation` would crash the editor/project because the `TextServer` that is used in `GDScriptParser::parse_identifier` and the `ScriptServer` that handles global classes were not loaded yet. Additionally, text `Translation`s would not load since the `ResourceFormatLoaderText` was not loaded yet. Therefore, I think the loading order of `TranslationServer`-related tasks should be moved after the global classes are set up.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101764/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101764/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}